l development. Staff training (Prong 1) delivered to all educational staff in first half-term (2 hours) with refresher annually (1 hour) = 3 hours training per annum. Prong 2 delivered within existing 30 hours SLT allocation + additional 5 hours annually for non-literal language intervention and safeguarding-focused teaching (TOTAL: 35 hours SLT per annum across all Communication & Interaction needs). LSA reinforces Prong 2 teaching through weekly practice activities (15 minutes per session integrated into existing 40-minute weekly sessions). Parents provided with idiom reference guide and communication strategies</em></strong><br><br><strong><em>✓ Session length/frequency: Staff training (Prong 1) in first half-term (2 hours) + annual refresher (1 hour). Prong 1 implementation is continuous across all adult interactions with Amelia. SLT delivers Prong 2 across 5 hours annually in sessions of 30-60 minutes (approximately 6-10 sessions per year) depending on Amelia's capacity. LSA delivers 15 minutes weekly practice. Idiom/phrase reference guide updated termly as new relevant phrases identified</em></strong><br><br><strong><em>✓ When reviewed: Prong 1 (environmental modifications) reviewed termly through staff feedback and parent consultation - are adults consistently using clear language? Prong 2 (skill development) progress tracked by LSA using comprehension accuracy data on taught items (weekly logs). SLT conducts formal receptive language reassessment annually using standardized assessments. Formal review half-termly at MDT meetings. SAFEGUARDING REVIEW: Annual review of whether literal interpretation has led to any vulnerable situations, with program adjustments as needed</em></strong><br><br><strong><em>Rationale: This provision prioritizes SAFETY through environmental modification while simultaneously building Amelia's skills. The two-pronged approach recognizes that expecting Amelia to fully overcome literal interpretation is unrealistic given her ASD diagnosis, but she can learn strategies. The safeguarding-specific component is ESSENTIAL given explicit mention of social vulnerability in the need. This provision directly supports outcome E1(iii) but extends beyond it to address the real-world functional and safety implications</em></strong></div>
