ection - 1 hour consultation)</em></strong><br><br><strong><em>✓ Session length/frequency: Environmental optimization and scaffolds provided continuously throughout all educational interactions. No separate "attention training" sessions - provision embedded within all activities. SLT metacognitive strategy teaching occurs within regular SLT sessions across the year (approximately 2 hours total embedded time). Staff training in Term 1 (2 hours)</em></strong><br><br><strong><em>✓ When reviewed: Daily monitoring via wellbeing tier system (NEED 5) indicates attention capacity. Tutors note in session records when attention difficulties impact learning. Formal review at half-termly MDT meetings examining patterns (which contexts, times, tasks most affect attention) to inform provision adjustments. Annual review of whether supports are adequate</em></strong><br><br><strong><em>Rationale: The need explicitly states attention is "most significantly" affected by physical health and emotional state - therefore medical/wellbeing management is primary intervention (see other sections). This Communication & Interaction provision focuses on accommodating variable attention rather than "fixing" it, which is realistic given the underlying causes. Environmental and scaffold supports are evidence-based for ADHD (Amelia's diagnosis). Avoids stigmatizing separate "attention training" which would be inappropriate given attention variation is secondary to pain and anxiety</em></strong></div>
