s not account for the variability and severity of CRPS pain flares described in the need; (3) "Request support with personal care and mobility" is minimal compared to the need's description of being wheelchair-bound and unable to get out of bed during severe periods; (4) There are no measures related to pain management, environmental adaptations, or functional mobility during different phases of CRPS. This should be redesigned to include: specific supports during pain flares, environmental adaptations for wheelchair access, pain management strategies with measurable outcomes, functional mobility goals across different pain levels, and realistic expectations for engagement that account for severe pain episodes.</em></div>
